{#-
  The agent exchange, on the page about connecting one (moved from the
  front page, Jamie 2026-11-12: "moving the agent demo and counts to Docs
  and Status"). A layout piece, not Markdown: the docs corpus an agent
  reads and llms-full.txt render a page's Markdown alone, and an agent has
  no use for a typing window. The three exchanges are the examples'
  own (_data/transcript.js), so this and /examples cannot disagree.
-#}
<section class="doc-demo" aria-labelledby="ask-in-plain-language">
  <h2 id="ask-in-plain-language">Ask in plain language</h2>
  <p>
    Your agent gets the tools, what your account allows, and every answer
    with its sample size. You ask the way you would ask a clanmate; the
    answer comes from the record, with the numbers behind it.
  </p>
  {%- set scripts = transcript %}
  {% include "transcript.njk" %}
  <p class="footnote">
    A real exchange, recorded Sep 10: each question was put to the live
    service, the tools under the window are the ones that answered it, and
    every number came back from them.
  </p>
  <p class="doc-demo__links">
    <a href="#connect">Connect your agent ›</a>
    <a href="/examples/play">Every example, start to finish ›</a>
  </p>
</section>
<script defer src="{{ "/assets/transcript.js" | asset }}"></script>
